  "description": "Panel power analyser with RS485 Modbus RTU: present, maximum and minimum values of voltages, currents, powers, power factor, frequency and THD, energies and current harmonics",
  "revision": 3,
  "revised": "2026-11-13",
  "source": "Circutor, Supply network analyzer CVM-144 series instruction manual (version 6.11 and higher), M98170101-03, section 11.4 MODBUS protocol",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Supply network analyzer CVM-144 series, instruction manual (Ver 6.11 and higher)",
      "version": "M98170101-03",
      "url": "https://docs.circutor.com/docs/M98170101-03.pdf",
      "note": "section 11.4, Modbus registers, example and relay/input functions"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Circutor CVM-144 (firmware 6.11 and later). Registers of section 11.4 of the manual.",
    "Each parameter is a 32-bit value in two registers, high word first (as in the manual's example). Functions 03 and 04 both read them; at most 20 parameters per request.",
    "Units follow the manual: voltages in V x 10, currents in mA, powers in W and var, power factor and cos phi x 100, frequency and THD x 10, energies in Wh and varh.",
    "Relay outputs are read with function 01 from 0 and written with function 05; the digital inputs of the input module are read with function 01 from 0x10.",
    "Not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
